# TTC (Tool Terse Catalog) — this repo's mct-mcp-server tool descriptions.
#
# Format: one block per tool, blocks separated by one or more blank lines.
#   TOOL <name>
#   WHEN <one line: when an agent should reach for this tool>
#   ERR  <one line: what NOT to use it for / caveats / failure modes>
#   TAGS <comma-separated short keywords, for discovery/matching>
#   PRE  <contract: what must hold before calling (required args, scope)>
#   POST <contract: what a successful call returns>
#   EFFECTS <none|read|write>; <what it touches>
#
# PRE/POST/EFFECTS are the tool's contract (issue #17). They stay out of the
# `description` (the catalog's byte budget); EFFECTS sets the MCP
# readOnlyHint/destructiveHint annotations, `batch` refuses any tool whose
# class isn't none/read, and get_tool_schema shows the full contract.
#
# Every field may appear in any order after the TOOL line, but each must
# appear exactly once, on a single line (no wrapping/continuation). Lines
# outside a block, and blank lines, are ignored as separators/comments —
# except a line starting with `#`, which is a comment anywhere.
#
# Parsed by crates/mct-mcp-server/src/ttc.rs at server startup and expanded
# into the `description` string installed on each tool in the rmcp catalog
# (see MctServer::new). Add a block here whenever a tool is added; the
# #[tool(description = "...")] attribute in server.rs only needs a short
# fallback string used if this file ever fails to parse or a tool name here
# doesn't match a registered tool. Keep WHEN/ERR terse — this file's whole
# purpose is a compact catalog, not restated prose.

TOOL list_symbols
WHEN symbols in a file or dir/crate prefix, before you know a name.
ERR not for a known symbol's definition — use find_symbol.
TAGS discovery, symbols, list, file, directory, crate
PRE `path` non-blank, relative to the project root.
POST symbols under that file or dir/crate prefix, capped by `limit`.
EFFECTS read; index only.

TOOL find_symbol
WHEN locate a symbol's definition; exact/prefix/fuzzy match, any language.
ERR not for callers/references — use find_callers/find_references.
TAGS lookup, definition, location, exact, prefix, fuzzy
PRE `name` non-blank.
POST matching definitions with path:line, or a no-match note.
EFFECTS read; index only.

TOOL search_symbols
WHEN unsure of a name: words/partial ident in any case style, BM25-ranked, exact first.
ERR not exhaustive (use find_symbol/list_symbols); not relations (use find_references).
TAGS search, ranked, words, camelCase, snake_case, partial
PRE `query` non-blank.
POST a ranked page (`offset`/`limit`), exact name first; optional snippets.
EFFECTS read; index, project files for snippets, query cache.

TOOL hybrid_search
WHEN find code by meaning: search_symbols + embeddings, RRF-fused; alpha 0=lexical..1=semantic (auto if omitted); "quoted" query = exact phrase, lexical only, also lists string literals (error/log messages) holding it as path:line.
ERR no model -> lexical only (noted); not exhaustive.
TAGS semantic, embeddings, hybrid
PRE `query` non-blank; `alpha` in 0..1 if given.
POST a ranked page; first line notes a lexical-only fallback.
EFFECTS read; index, project files, query cache; may download the embedding model once.

TOOL find_references
WHEN every reference to a symbol: calls, imports, extends/implements.
ERR not just direct callers (use find_callers); not a definition lookup (use find_symbol).
TAGS references, calls, imports, broad
PRE `symbol` non-blank.
POST every indexed reference with path:line, paged by `offset`/`limit`.
EFFECTS read; index only.

TOOL find_calls
WHEN what a function/method calls — its callees.
ERR not who calls it — use find_callers.
TAGS callees, outgoing, calls
PRE `function` non-blank.
POST its indexed callees with path:line.
EFFECTS read; index only.

TOOL find_callers
WHEN who directly calls a function/method.
ERR not broader refs (use find_references); not full blast radius (use impact_analysis).
TAGS callers, incoming, calls
PRE `function` non-blank.
POST its indexed direct callers with path:line.
EFFECTS read; index only.

TOOL impact_analysis
WHEN full blast radius before changing/removing a symbol: callers+refs+likely tests.
ERR not for just callers or just refs — cheaper via find_callers/find_references alone.
TAGS impact, blast-radius, composite, tests
PRE `symbol` non-blank.
POST callers, references and likely tests, each section capped.
EFFECTS read; index only.

TOOL build_context_pack
WHEN before working on a symbol: def+doc+source, callers/callees/deps/tests once each.
ERR not blast radius (use impact_analysis); ambiguous name -> path/language.
TAGS context, composite, tests, tokens-saving
PRE `symbol` non-blank; `path`/`language` disambiguate.
POST definitions with source, then each related symbol once; ambiguous callees apart.
EFFECTS read; index, project files, query cache.

TOOL reindex
WHEN force an immediate refresh now; force=true bypasses the hash check.
ERR no symbol data; already runs at startup and in the background.
TAGS index, refresh, admin, force
PRE none; `force` optional.
POST a summary of files indexed, skipped and failed.
EFFECTS write; rewrites .mct-index from project files; refused inside batch.

TOOL get_indexing_status
WHEN index health: files/symbols per language, last run, parse failures, deps.
ERR no symbol data — use find_symbol.
TAGS index, status, health, diagnostics
PRE none.
POST per-language counts, last run, parse failures.
EFFECTS read; index only.

TOOL get_file_skeleton
WHEN a file's top-level shape, bodies collapsed to `// ...`.
ERR single file only (use list_symbols for dirs); no real impl (use find_symbol then read).
TAGS skeleton, shape, file, tokens-saving
PRE `path` non-blank, one file inside the project root.
POST top-level declarations, bodies collapsed.
EFFECTS read; index and that file.

TOOL get_project_overview
WHEN get oriented in an unfamiliar file/dir/crate/project fast, ranked digest.
ERR not a precise lookup (use find_symbol); not uncapped (use list_symbols).
TAGS overview, digest, orientation, tokens-saving
PRE none; `path` scopes it.
POST a capped, ranked digest.
EFFECTS read; index only.

TOOL find_dead_code
WHEN top-level symbols with zero indexed references — dead-code candidates.
ERR heuristic only; verify with find_references/impact_analysis before deleting.
TAGS dead-code, unused, cleanup, heuristic
PRE none; `path`/`language` scope it.
POST top-level symbols with zero indexed references.
EFFECTS read; index only.

TOOL get_file_tree
WHEN plain directory/file layout before you know which file or crate to look at.
ERR no symbol data — use list_symbols/get_project_overview for what's defined.
TAGS layout, directory, tree, navigation, tokens-saving
PRE none; `path` scopes it.
POST a depth-limited directory tree.
EFFECTS read; project directory listing.

TOOL discover_tool_categories
WHEN first call in a session — names+one-line purpose per tool, grouped, no schemas.
ERR no input schemas here — call get_tool_schema per tool name before invoking it.
TAGS discovery, catalog, categories, progressive, tokens-saving
PRE none.
POST every tool name and purpose, grouped.
EFFECTS none; serves the static catalog.

TOOL get_tool_schema
WHEN full input schema+description for one tool named by discover_tool_categories.
ERR not a symbol lookup; unknown tool name is an error, not a fuzzy match.
TAGS discovery, schema, progressive, meta
PRE `name` is a registered tool.
POST its description, contract and input schema.
EFFECTS none; serves the static catalog.

TOOL batch
WHEN several known read-only queries at once: [{tool,args}], one result per [n] header.
ERR no reindex/nested batch; a failed query is reported inline, the rest still run.
TAGS batch, multiple, tokens-saving, composite
PRE 1..25 `queries`, each naming a read-only tool.
POST one [n] section per query; failures inline.
EFFECTS read; runs read-only tools only, never a nested batch.

TOOL select_tools
WHEN first, with the user's request: narrows tools/list to the tools it needs.
ERR picks, never runs; unclear request -> full list; all tools stay callable.
TAGS attention, intent, selection, tokens-saving
PRE `query` non-empty; only with MCT_TOOL_ATTENTION=1.
POST the intent, the picked tool names and argument hints.
EFFECTS write; replaces this session's advertised tools/list; refused inside batch.
